-- Tests added in pass 2 for the refusals that replaced FALSE in `bc-interpretation-definitions.l4` (s 24). The cases that
-- pass 1 already tested were changed in place in `bc-tests-definitions.l4`; these are the cases it did not test.
-- Each expected value was decided from the text before the file was first run.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-definitions`


§ `s 24 Documentary evidence: an enactment that provides no evidence rule`
-- 24 begins "If an enactment provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact": with no such provision the section says nothing, whatever the context.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 24 the fact is deemed to be established` FALSE FALSE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 24 the fact is deemed to be established` FALSE FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 24 the fact is deemed to be established` FALSE TRUE FALSE
        BECAUSE "s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 24 the document is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` FALSE TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 24 speaks only of an enactment that provides that a document is evidence or proof of a fact"

